      "category": "material",
      "title": "Code Example: Python Bisection Search",
      "presentationSlot": "current",
      "createdAt": 1721243715000,
      "description": "{\"html\":\"<div style=\\\"font-family: monospace; background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;\\\">\\n  <h3 style=\\\"color: #569cd6; margin-top:0;\\\">def bisection_search(L, e):</h3>\\n  <pre style=\\\"white-space: pre-wrap; background: #2d2d2d; border: 1px solid #333; padding: 10px;\\\">low = 0\\nhigh = len(L) - 1\\nwhile low &lt;= high:\\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\\n    if L[mid] == e:\\n        return True\\n    elif L[mid] &lt; e:\\n        low = mid + 1\\n    else:\\n        high = mid - 1\\nreturn False</pre>\\n  <p style=\\\"color: #9cdcfe;\\\">Static, read-only example. Use an institution-approved coding tool for executable labs.</p>\\n</div>\",\"css\":\"\",\"js\":\"\"}"
    },
